{"name":"Key Lime","hex":"#aeff6e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"key lime","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Key lime."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/key_lime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Key lime","blocks":[{"text":"The Key lime, also known as West Indian lime, Mexican lime, or Egyptian lime is a type of lime. While it is treated as a species in botanical classification, it originated as a natural hybrid between Citrus micrantha and Citrus medica (citron)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia_%28Christm.%29_Swingle_%2851906868474%29.jpg/330px-Citrus_%C3%97_aurantiifolia_%28Christm.%29_Swingle_%2851906868474%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Key_lime","wikidata":"Q165354"},{"title":"Lime (fruit)","blocks":[{"text":"A lime is the fruit of several species of citrus, most of which are hybrids within the genus Citrus. Limes are generally small, round to oval fruits with green flesh and skin and a distinctly sour taste due to their high citric acid content. They are widely cultivated in tropical and subtropical regions for culinary, medicinal, and ornamental purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Lime_Blossom.jpg/330px-Lime_Blossom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(fruit)","wikidata":"Q13195"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)","wikidata":"Q906936"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/A_tree_full_of_key_limes_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg/500px-A_tree_full_of_key_limes_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/A_tree_full_of_key_limes_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg/1280px-A_tree_full_of_key_limes_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/A_tree_full_of_key_limes_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg/500px-A_tree_full_of_key_limes_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A tree full of key limes in West Bengal, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_tree_full_of_key_limes_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Dayap_or_Philippine_keylime.jpg/500px-Dayap_or_Philippine_keylime.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Dayap_or_Philippine_keylime.jpg/1280px-Dayap_or_Philippine_keylime.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Dayap_or_Philippine_keylime.jpg/500px-Dayap_or_Philippine_keylime.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Key lime is known as dayap in the Philippines, where it is native","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADayap_or_Philippine_keylime.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Keylime-flower.jpg/500px-Keylime-flower.jpg?utm_source=en.